<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James III of Scotland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1452–1488</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James III was king of Scots from 1460 to 1488, succeeding as a child after his father James II was killed at the siege of Roxburgh. His marriage to Margaret of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shetland">Shetland</a> to the Scottish crown in pledge for her dowry in 1468–1469, and they were annexed in 1472. Unpopular with his nobles, he was killed after the Battle of Sauchieburn.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-iii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="James III of Scotland" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hugo van der Goes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugo_van_der_Goes_-_The_Trinity_Altarpiece_-_James_III_of_Scotland_accompanied_by_his_son_James,_presented_by_St_Andrew_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
